  "problem": "CDC catalog entries mixed tabular datasets with documents, visualizations and external links. Field extraction could run before view identity was verified, treat a dashboard as a queryable table, infer geography completeness or person-level grain from PLACES columns, or drop isolated records.",
  "resulting_behavior": "bindCdcView verifies the Socrata view id before extracting columns. Tabular table views stay in the row-sample queue. Documents (blobby), visualizations (story/chart/map) and external links (href) stay out and are not queryable tables. PLACES county GIS 2023 (7cmc-7y5g) produces 154 documented fields without geography completeness or person-level grain. buildCdcExtractionReceipt reconciles all 1472 CDC IDs; none disappear. The four empty-description isolated records remain in compatibility/missing-data handling. Dictionary counts use record IDs with parse receipts, not fetched pages. HTTP 200 HTML cannot be JSON success. Live fetch is forbidden.",
  "commits": [
    {
      "id": "C-014-1",
